	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Type yt in Alfred to choose a command, or type a command directly:

- yt or yt toggle: toggle playback
- yt play: resume playback
- yt pause: pause playback
- yt next: skip to the next track
- yt prev: select the previous track
- yt status: show the current track and playback state

Aliases: resume, previous, back, playpause.

Keep YouTube Music open in a Chrome PWA or tab. Controls run in the background without activating Chrome or the PWA. If several YouTube Music tabs are open, the first matching tab is used.

In a regular Chrome window using the same profile as the PWA, enable View &gt; Developer &gt; Allow JavaScript from Apple Events. macOS may also ask you to allow Alfred to control Google Chrome.

The control external trigger accepts the same canonical command names.</string>
